                    <signifLet xml:id="m-f7de8aee-5f49-4614-8f71-acbf985f7008" /></nc></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-8bcba8b3-b21b-43a0-a6a3-52b3fe57c39a">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-5fc0fa55-2af0-4b7e-aaf8-ae7441dd5a84" type="punctum" xml:id="m-b499941a-2482-49a1-900f-c40f4841f1c2">
                  <nc xml:id="m-6fb70653-4d79-4070-a1b7-4adee3311124" pname="a" oct="3">
                    <signifLet xml:id="m-628c91aa-9de8-4b74-bd50-731425021ead" /></nc></neume></syllable><divLine xml:id="m-616ed0b9-bd85-41bd-911b-4c254698fdc1" facs="#m-1b60782b-af2a-4af6-9c91-330957d29765" form="finalis" /></layer></staff><div xml:id="m-bea8a208-606c-4f36-a873-5a37e87dab3e">
            <lg xml:id="m-11751ea4-b556-4ca2-97e4-1a7b4d1d26df">
              <l xml:id="m-b832ea2d-f632-4e52-bc30-79b7a45ec73a" facs="#m-7f1b4c4e-21d8-47c7-b051-a1b8a94af7b4" label="ambiguous">121</l><l xml:id="m-1b8016b5-4fd9-4518-a09c-7bb17ca2575e" facs="#m-860b35d0-dabf-4b8e-91a5-07333a762b92" label="text-like">Tones for the Lessons.</l><l xml:id="m-e2a7835b-2635-41ea-b6d0-809a849ceca9" facs="#m-e5cfcd4c-94b8-4630-b9a9-ecb1114ff5fb" label="text-like">This tone has the flex and the metrum. However, if the sentence is short</l><l xml:id="m-f9bdc6e8-073b-4835-a82a-b7134791174a" facs="#m-00252533-3f93-4e9a-bbb4-c14749f1514a" label="text-like">or if the sense does not allow it, the flex may be suppressed. and even the</l><l xml:id="m-25e0ae23-a09a-4e2f-95dd-80a1c7df340f" facs="#m-df59eea2-2767-4e72-a43a-5d8a9e2dc7bc" label="text-like">metrum. The fex must not be used without the metrum; but the metrum</l><l xml:id="m-19d2f707-bc27-4a55-aa0c-58c99ae93c11" facs="#m-591dfd66-5af9-4712-9bbd-973516b7092d" label="text-like">may be used without the fex. In long sentences, the fex and the metrum</l><l xml:id="m-8ad9d61a-7c80-47c3-b23f-fdb6d242b501" facs="#m-b508bf8a-dd86-4ba7-aed7-c5be44c588df" label="ambiguous">may be repeated, alternately, several times.</l><l xml:id="m-77573cef-a83e-459f-920c-ca2e791166e9" facs="#m-2592ca25-7c6f-4564-8427-ca23f42a2087" label="text-like">The fiex is always made by lowering the voice a minor third, even if u</l><l xml:id="m-3435ed7e-aedf-479b-a69d-503429e57367" facs="#m-365a47cc-3831-49e2-852c-85cc709a5a54" label="text-like">occur at a monosyllable or a Hebrew word.</l><l xml:id="m-0bc3a479-51d7-4242-b6d0-6a1779ba9878" facs="#m-ea8410b3-99b5-4d6c-ae35-a796a08a97f5" label="text-like">The interrogation is made as indicated on pp. 103-104; so also is the final</l><l xml:id="m-c3e502b1-a58f-43f0-84eb-3bfbfcbf27c1" facs="#m-e56c6e64-e9eb-4fc1-a74c-6ec1702d14ee" label="text-like">formula when not followed br the conclusion Tu autem.</l><l xml:id="m-2c5645d2-e188-49d7-9dc7-cf649f5d9b9c" facs="#m-7932878b-5d4d-